on-symbol><classification-symbol scheme="EC">B60W  20/00</classification-symbol></classification-ecla><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="EN">BRAKE DEVICE FOR CAR</invention-title><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">DISPOSITIF DE FREINAGE POUR AUTOMOBILE</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-5284607-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5284607</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7163008-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7163008</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-9074605-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9074605</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-9154202-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>9154202</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9289705-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9289705</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1092584A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISSAN DIESEL</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA JUN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA YOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISSAN DIESEL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, JUN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA JUN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA YOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, JUN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A brake device for cars comprising a motor for moving a car and a battery as a power source wherein the regenerative braking force of the motor is maximally produced. A required braking force (BO) is defined by BO = BFO + BRO - BFm where BM is the regenerative braking force produced by the motor, BB is the braking force corresponding to the amount of fed electricity acceptable by the battery, BFO is the braking force on the driven wheel side according to the amount of braking operation, BRO is the braking force on the driving wheel side, and BFm is the requisite minimum of braking force on the driven wheel side. Control is made as follows: the regenerative braking force (BM) of the motor is set at BM when BB&gt;/=BM, and at BB when BB &lt; BM. When BM&gt;/=BO, the braking force on the driven wheel side is set at BFm and the braking force of the motor is set at BO. When BM &lt; BO, the braking force is set at BFm, the regenerative force of the motor is set at BM, and for the shortage, the braking mechanism of the car compensates for the braking force.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de freinage pour automobiles comprenant un moteur permettant leur déplacement et une batterie faisant office de source d'énergie, la force de freinage électrodynamique par régénération produite par le moteur étant maximale. La force de freinage requise (BO) est définie par BO = BFO + BRO BFM, BM représentant la force de freinage électrodynamique par régénération produite par le moteur, BB la force de freinage correspondant à la quantité d'électricité fournie acceptable par la batterie, BFO la force de freinage du côté roues menées en fonction de l'ampleur de l'opération de freinage, BRO la force de freinage du côté roues d'entraînement et BFM la force de freinage minimum du côté roues menées. La régulation s'effectue de la manière suivante: la force de freinage électrodynamique par régénération (BM) du moteur est fixée à BM lorsque BB&gt;/=BM, et à BB lorsque BB &lt; BM. Lorsque BM&gt;/=BO, la force de freinage du côté roues menées est fixée à BFM et la force de freinage du moteur est fixée à BO. Lorsque BM &lt; BO, la force de freinage est fixée à BFM, la force régénératrice du moteur est fixée à BM, et en cas de déficit, le mécanisme de freinage de l'automobile compense la force de freinage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>